From 17288241a32473949caf3b1115d06a5972fab915 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Braga?= <code@andrebraga.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:25:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: advertise how many links a station runs at once

ath12k fills the MLD capabilities of the AP interface type from the
firmware and leaves the station's at zero, so a station tells AP MLDs it
runs a single link at a time. It still sets up a link to every affiliated
AP the supplicant asks for, then activates one per radio. With an AP MLD
on more bands than the device has radios, the extra links are set up but
never active. On a WCN7860 with a tri-band AP MLD, three-link
associations never completed the 4-way handshake and timed out with
reason 4, while the same association with two links completes.

Set the station's maximum number of simultaneous links to the radios of
the hardware group, so the AP and the supplicant can size the link set.

Tested-on: WCN7860 hw2.0 PCI WLAN.GNG.1.0-04065-QCAGNGSWPL_V1.0_V2.0_SILICONZ-1
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
index bc92a66dd..0a1721134 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -15146,8 +15146,21 @@ static int ath12k_mac_hw_register(struct ath12k_hw *ah)
 	 * WMI_SERVICE_READY_EXT2_EVENT if single_chip_mlo_supp is set.
 	 */
 	if (ab->ag->mlo_capable) {
+		u8 num_links = 0;
+
 		ath12k_iftypes_ext_capa[2].eml_capabilities = cap->eml_cap;
 		ath12k_iftypes_ext_capa[2].mld_capa_and_ops = cap->mld_cap;
+
+		/* A station runs one link per radio of the group at a time.
+		 * Tell the AP, so it does not count on links that are set up
+		 * but never active.
+		 */
+		for (i = 0; i < ab->ag->num_devices; i++)
+			num_links += ab->ag->ab[i]->qmi.num_radios;
+		ath12k_iftypes_ext_capa[1].mld_capa_and_ops =
+			u16_encode_bits(num_links - 1,
+					IEEE80211_MLD_CAP_OP_MAX_SIMUL_LINKS);
+
 		wiphy->flags |= WIPHY_FLAG_SUPPORTS_MLO;
 
 		ieee80211_hw_set(hw, MLO_MCAST_MULTI_LINK_TX);
-- 
